      "message": "Two things:\n1. Why is this hidden? The other keys in this namespace are APIs.\n2. The format of this key is FAR too fragile and poorly defined.  It should be restructured in a persistable bundle style key with well defined values.  \n\nI can envision a KEY_ERROR_POLICY_CONFIG_PERSISTABLE_BUNDLE defined with sub-keys keys like KEY_CAPABILITIES_STRING_ARRAY (for the ims|eims), KEY_ERROR_TYPE_INT (For the error types like GENERIC_ERROR_TYPE which would be defined using an intdef), KEY_ERROR_NUMBER_INT - for single error code, KEY_ERROR_NuMBER_RANGE_INT_ARRAY - for errors in range, KEY_MATCH_ALL_ERROR_NUMBERS_BOOL - for matching all errors.\n\nThere should be some other persistable bundle keys which were added recently in here you can look at for inspiration.",
